### Send a new activity log
POST http://localhost:3000/api/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user123",
  "action": "LOGIN",
  "metadata": {
    "browser": "Chrome",
    "ip": "192.168.1.1"
  }
}

###

### Send another log
POST http://localhost:3000/api/logs
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "user456",
  "action": "PAGE_VIEW",
  "metadata": {
    "page": "/dashboard"
  }
}

###

### Get all logs
GET http://localhost:3000/api/logs

###

### Get logs filtered by userId
GET http://localhost:3000/api/logs?userId=user123

###

### Get logs with pagination
GET http://localhost:3000/api/logs?page=1&limit=5

###

### Health check
GET http://localhost:3000/health
```

Then in VS Code:
1. Open `test.http`
2. You'll see **"Send Request"** appear above each block
3. Click it on the first POST request

Watch your terminal — you should see:
```
Sent activity log for user: user123
Processed log | User: user123 | Action: LOGIN